{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-08-16T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Some landscapes are shaped not by people, but by the steady forces of nature over thousands of years. That's exactly the story of Pedra Furada in Jericoacoara, in the Brazilian state of Ceará. Wind and sea gradually carved this natural arch, which has become one of the region's most recognisable landmarks. Located within Jericoacoara National Park, the arch stands along the coast and frames the Atlantic Ocean. From July into early August, visitors gather to watch its most famous spectacle, when the setting sun aligns with the opening in the rock, shining through it for a few minutes before dipping below the horizon.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Furada_ROW7736094795_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Furada_ROW7736094795_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Pedra Furada, Jericoacoara, Brazil","Copyright":"© Brendan van Son/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260816_Furada\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Pedra+Furada+Brazil&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260816_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260816_Furada"},"Ssd":"20260816","Name":"Furada","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7736094795","FullDateString":"16 ago. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"At first glance, it's just a bridge. Then the reflection changes everything. Infinity Bridge spans the River Tees in Stockton-on-Tees, England, where its two striking steel arches and their reflections create the shape of an infinity symbol, inspiring its name. Opened in 2009, the pedestrian and cycle bridge was designed by Expedition Engineering with architect Spence Associates as part of the regeneration of the town's riverside. Stretching 240 metres, its tied-arch structure combines engineering efficiency with a distinctive visual identity.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.StocktonInfinity_ROW7557207458_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.StocktonInfinity_ROW7557207458_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Infinity Bridge in Stockton-on-Tees, England","Copyright":"© Bahadir Yeniceri/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260815_StocktonInfinity\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Infinity+Bridge+England&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260815_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260815_StocktonInfinity"},"Ssd":"20260815","Name":"StocktonInfinity","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7557207458","FullDateString":"15 ago. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"From above, Palmanova looks less like a town and more like a carefully drawn star set into the plains of Friuli-Venezia Giulia, Italy. Founded by the Republic of Venice in 1593, this fortress city was designed for defence, order and spectacle. Its streets radiate from a central square, while its walls are shaped into a precise nine-pointed pattern. That geometry was no accident. Palmanova became one of the most influential models of early modern military architecture. It was protected by concentric fortifications built first under Venice and later strengthened and expanded during the Napoleonic period.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Palmanova_ROW7371050659_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Palmanova_ROW7371050659_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Aerial view of Palmanova, a fortress city in Friuli, Italy","Copyright":"© Riccardo Saponi/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260814_Palmanova\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Palmanova+Italy&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260814_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260814_Palmanova"},"Ssd":"20260814","Name":"Palmanova","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7371050659","FullDateString":"14 ago. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"When darkness falls over Tenerife, Spain, the stars take centre stage. Perched high on the slopes of Mount Teide, Teide Observatory is one of the world's leading solar observatories and among the best places in Europe for astronomical research. Opened in 1964 at an altitude of about 2,390 metres, it benefits from clear skies, dry air and minimal light pollution for much of the year, making it ideal for observing the sun by day and the night sky after sunset.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PerseidasTenerife_ROW7214052413_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PerseidasTenerife_ROW7214052413_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Perseid meteors over Teide Observatory, Tenerife, Spain","Copyright":"© Westend61/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260813_PerseidasTenerife\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Teide+Observatory&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260813_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260813_PerseidasTenerife"},"Ssd":"20260813","Name":"PerseidasTenerife","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7214052413","FullDateString":"13 ago. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A line of elephants emerges from the morning haze, calves keeping pace beside older relatives as they head towards a marsh. In Amboseli National Park, scenes like this unfold every day, shaped by water hidden beneath the ground. Meltwater from Mount Kilimanjaro filters through volcanic rock before surfacing as springs that keep the park's wetlands alive, even when the surrounding plains are dry. These permanent water sources sustain elephants, buffaloes, hippos and many other animals, while acacia woodland and open grassland support predators such as lions and cheetahs.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ElephantDay_ROW7064675180_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ElephantDay_ROW7064675180_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"A group of elephants, Amboseli National Park, Kenya","Copyright":"© Ibrahim Suha Derbent/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260812_ElephantDay\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Amboseli+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260812_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260812_ElephantDay"},"Ssd":"20260812","Name":"ElephantDay","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7064675180","FullDateString":"12 ago. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Ships, storms and changing technology have come and gone, but the light remains. On Washington's San Juan Island, Lime Kiln Lighthouse has overlooked Haro Strait since 1919. Perched on a rocky bluff, its white flash continues to guide vessels through one of the Pacific Northwest's most important inland waterways. The lighthouse stands within Lime Kiln Point State Park, widely regarded as one of the world's best places to watch wild orcas from shore, with whales sometimes passing remarkably close to the coast.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LimeKiln_ROW6859587054_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LimeKiln_ROW6859587054_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Lime Kiln Lighthouse on San Juan Island, Washington state, United States","Copyright":"© Edmund Lowe Photography/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260811_LimeKiln\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lime+Kiln+Lighthouse&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260811_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260811_LimeKiln"},"Ssd":"20260811","Name":"LimeKiln","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6859587054","FullDateString":"11 ago. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The best route here isn't built with concrete. Instead, the tide reveals a rocky path leading from Whytecliff Park to Whyte Islet in West Vancouver, Canada. A few hours later, the sea quietly covers the crossing again, making timing part of the experience. This shoreline has drawn visitors for generations. The tide opens the path; wet rocks keep you humble. The reward is a sweeping view back towards the beach and the hillside homes of Gleneagles.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.WhyteCliffP_ROW6700227959_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.WhyteCliffP_ROW6700227959_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Whytecliff Park, West Vancouver, Canada","Copyright":"© Aolin Chen/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260810_WhyteCliffP\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Whytecliff+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260810_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260810_WhyteCliffP"},"Ssd":"20260810","Name":"WhyteCliffP","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6700227959","FullDateString":"10 ago. 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In Alaska, some of the world's wildest wildlife spectacles unfold far from cities and roads. At Katmai National Park, brown bears line the river, and when the salmon jump, the show begins. Created in 1918 after the dramatic 1912 Novarupta volcanic eruption, the park protects more than 16,000 square kilometres of wilderness, including active volcanoes, tundra and salmon-rich rivers.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.KatmaiBear_ROW4890016899_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.KatmaiBear_ROW4890016899_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Brown bear fishing in river, Katmai National Park, Alaska, United States","Copyright":"© Pal Hermansen/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260823_KatmaiBear\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Katmai+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260823_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260823_KatmaiBear"},"Ssd":"20260823","Name":"KatmaiBear","Market":"ROW","Hash":"4890016899","FullDateString":"23 ago. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"That quick glimpse of blue fluttering through a field has a story that begins much earlier, with a tiny caterpillar and a surprising survival trick. The common blue is found across Europe, North Africa and parts of Asia, feeding on flower nectar as an adult. It starts life as a small egg, often placed by a female on a host plant such as bird's-foot trefoil. The real surprise comes during its caterpillar stage, when ants play an unexpected role in its survival. After hatching, the caterpillar feeds on leaves before entering the next stage of its transformation. Along the way, it produces a sugary substance called honeydew that ants feed on. As a way of saying thanks, the ants may protect the caterpillar from predators.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.CommonBlue_ROW4481033991_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.CommonBlue_ROW4481033991_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Common blue butterfly, Devon, England","Copyright":"© Ross Hoddinott/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260822_CommonBlue\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Common+blue+butterfly&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260822_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260822_CommonBlue"},"Ssd":"20260822","Name":"CommonBlue","Market":"ROW","Hash":"4481033991","FullDateString":"22 ago. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Some mountain roads become destinations in their own right, and Julier Pass is one of them. This Swiss mountain pass rises to 2,284 metres and has linked Alpine valleys along a route used for nearly 2,000 years. Its story began long before modern traffic. No guardrails, no pavement—just a route used by Roman travellers, merchants and messengers. Archaeological finds near the summit, including countless coins and two Roman soapstone columns, suggest there was once a sanctuary or stopping place for those tackling the climb.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.JulierPass_ROW4042203913_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.JulierPass_ROW4042203913_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Winding road of Julier Pass, Switzerland","Copyright":"© Westend61/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260821_JulierPass\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Julier+Pass+Switzerland&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260821_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260821_JulierPass"},"Ssd":"20260821","Name":"JulierPass","Market":"ROW","Hash":"4042203913","FullDateString":"21 ago. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"An orca breaks the surface of Lynn Canal against the backdrop of the snow-capped Chilkat Mountains in Southeast Alaska, United States. Also known as the killer whale, the orca is the largest member of the dolphin family and one of the ocean's most recognisable predators. Alaska's Inside Passage provides abundant feeding grounds, sustaining salmon runs and a rich variety of marine life that supports these remarkable animals.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.LynnCanalOrca_ROW8459582696_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.LynnCanalOrca_ROW8459582696_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"An orca surfaces in Lynn Canal near the Chilkat Mountains, Alaska, United States","Copyright":"© John Hyde/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260820_LynnCanalOrca\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Orca+animal&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260820_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260820_LynnCanalOrca"},"Ssd":"20260820","Name":"LynnCanalOrca","Market":"ROW","Hash":"8459582696","FullDateString":"20 ago. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Where two great deserts meet, Joshua Tree National Park reveals a stark, mesmerising landscape shaped by wind, time and extremes. In Southern California, the higher Mojave Desert merges with the hotter, lower Colorado Desert, creating a unique blend of ecosystems and remarkable biodiversity.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SandPath_ROW8239489384_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SandPath_ROW8239489384_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Joshua Tree National Park, California, United States","Copyright":"© JJ Landscapes/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260819_SandPath\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Joshua+Tree+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260819_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260819_SandPath"},"Ssd":"20260819","Name":"SandPath","Market":"ROW","Hash":"8239489384","FullDateString":"19 ago. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Roads have made travel faster for people but created new challenges for wildlife. Highways often cut across their regular migration routes, increasing collisions, fragmenting habitats and isolating animal populations. Wildlife crossings, also known as ecoducts, were developed to reconnect these landscapes. They include vegetated bridges over roads and tunnels beneath them, allowing animals to cross safely while reducing the risk of vehicle collisions. Some of the earliest modern examples appeared in France during the 1950s, while the Netherlands later expanded the idea with wide, green bridges designed to blend into the surrounding landscape.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.WildlifeCrossingPoland_ROW8094277128_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.WildlifeCrossingPoland_ROW8094277128_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Aerial view of a wildlife crossing near Zakrzów, Poland","Copyright":"© bbsferrari/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260818_WildlifeCrossingPoland\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Wildlife+crossing&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260818_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260818_WildlifeCrossingPoland"},"Ssd":"20260818","Name":"WildlifeCrossingPoland","Market":"ROW","Hash":"8094277128","FullDateString":"18 ago. 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Location matters. Just ask the false clownfish seen in the image at Lighthouse Reef, near Cabilao Island, Philippines. In these tropical waters packed with hungry mouths and fierce competition, they've secured prime real estate: a sea anemone armed with thousands of microscopic stinging cells.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.CabilaoClowns_ROW7942921985_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.CabilaoClowns_ROW7942921985_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Three false clownfish in a sea anemone, Cabilao Island, Bohol, Philippines","Copyright":"© Franco Banfi/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260817_CabilaoClowns\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=False+clownfish&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260817_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260817_CabilaoClowns"},"Ssd":"20260817","Name":"CabilaoClowns","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7942921985","FullDateString":"17 ago. 2026"}],"LocStrings":{"LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD":"Imagem do dia","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD_LEARN_MORE":"Saber mais","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_DONATE_NOW":"Doar agora","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_FACT":"Facto rápido:","LOC_HOMEPAGE_GALLERY_CARD_TITLE":"Imagens recentes da Home Page","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_GALLERY_IMAGE_ARIALABEL":"Imagem da home page de {0}","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ON_THIS_DAY_TITLE":"Neste dia na história","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ON_THIS_DAY_IMAGE_ARIALABEL":"Neste dia em {0}, {1}","LOC_HOMEPAGE_SHARE_TOOLTIP":"Partilhar a home page do Bing de hoje","LOC_HOMEPAGE_WALLPAPERDOWNLOAD_TOOLTIP":"Transfira esta imagem. Esta imagem só pode ser utilizada como padrão de fundo.","LOC_MUSCARD_DOWNLOAD_LINK":"Transferir esta imagem","LOC_HOMEPAGE_WALLPAPERNOTAVAILABLE":"Esta imagem não está disponível para transferência como papel de fun